1. GOAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Automate one LinkedIn post per day on Tony's personal account, covering:
  - Startup life
  - Cybersecurity
  - Coding / engineering
  - Corporate / B2B tech

The system generates a draft, notifies Tony, lets him preview and approve,
and posts automatically if he doesn't respond within a timeout window.


2. HIGH-LEVEL ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  [Cron] --> [Groq: draft] --> [Flask API: save + token] --> [ntfy: notify]
                                                                   |
                                                                   v
                                                            [Tony's phone]
                                                                   |
                                          +------------------------+----------------------+
                                          |                                               |
                                    [Preview page]                                  [No action]
                                          |                                               |
                                    [Approve tap]                                   [30 min timeout]
                                          |                                               |
                                          v                                               v
                                    [n8n resumes]                              [Gemini: proofread]
                                          |                                               |
                                          +----------------------+------------------------+
                                                                 |
                                                                 v
                                                          [LinkedIn post]
                                                                 |
                                                                 v
                                                     [Flask API: mark posted]


3. COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

COMPONENT         WHERE                    ROLE
----------------  -----------------------  --------------------------------------
n8n               Server (Docker)          Orchestrator, runs daily loop
Flask API         Server (same box)        Drafts, state, preview page, approvals
SQLite            Server                   Stores topics and drafts
Groq API          Cloud (free tier)        Generates first draft
Gemini API        Cloud (free tier)        Proofreads and corrects draft
ntfy              ntfy.sh (or self-hosted) Push notification to phone
LinkedIn node     Inside n8n               Posts to Tony's personal LinkedIn


4. DAILY FLOW (n8n WORKFLOW)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 1 — TRIGGER
  Node:     Cron
  Fires:    Once daily, 09:00 EAT
  Output:   None, kicks the flow

STEP 2 — PICK TOPIC
  Node:     HTTP Request
  Method:   GET
  URL:      https://yourdomain.com/api/next-topic
  Header:   Authorization: Bearer <N8N_SECRET>
  Returns:  { "topic_id": 12, "category": "cybersec",
              "prompt": "Why zero-trust matters for East African fintechs" }

STEP 3 — GENERATE DRAFT
  Node:     Groq Chat Model
  Model:    llama-3.3-70b-versatile (or similar)
  Prompt:   "Write a LinkedIn post for a Kenyan B2B software CEO.
             Topic: {{prompt}}. Category: {{category}}.
             Tone: direct, technical, no fluff. Max 200 words. No hashtags."
  Output:   Draft text

STEP 4 — SAVE DRAFT
  Node:     HTTP Request
  Method:   POST
  URL:      https://yourdomain.com/api/drafts
  Header:   Authorization: Bearer <N8N_SECRET>
  Body:     {
              "topic_id": 12,
              "category": "cybersec",
              "body": "<draft text>",
              "n8n_resume_url": "<Wait node webhook URL>"
            }
  Returns:  {
              "draft_id": 42,
              "token": "abc123...",
              "preview_url": "https://yourdomain.com/preview/abc123..."
            }

STEP 5 — NOTIFY
  Node:     HTTP Request
  Method:   POST
  URL:      https://ntfy.sh/<private-topic>
  Body:     "New draft ready: <first 60 chars>"
  Header:   Actions: view, Preview, https://yourdomain.com/preview/abc123...

STEP 6 — WAIT FOR APPROVAL
  Node:     Wait (webhook mode)
  Timeout:  30 minutes
  Behavior: - If Flask API hits webhook with ?approved=true --> approved branch
            - If 30 min pass with no hit                    --> timeout branch

STEP 7a — APPROVED BRANCH
  Node:     LinkedIn (n8n native)
  Action:   Create Post
  Text:     <draft body>
  Then:     Step 8

STEP 7b — TIMEOUT BRANCH
  Node:     Google Gemini
  Model:    gemini-2.0-flash (or similar)
  Prompt:   "Proofread this LinkedIn post. Fix grammar and spelling.
             Return only the corrected text. Do not change meaning or style.
             Post: <draft body>"
  Then:     LinkedIn node --> post
  Then:     Step 8

STEP 8 — MARK POSTED
  Node:     HTTP Request
  Method:   POST
  URL:      https://yourdomain.com/api/drafts/42/posted
  Header:   Authorization: Bearer <N8N_SECRET>
  Effect:   Flips status to "posted", logs timestamp


5. FLASK API SPEC
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ROUTE                              METHOD  AUTH         PURPOSE
---------------------------------  ------  -----------  --------------------------
/api/next-topic                    GET     bearer       Pop next unused topic
/api/drafts                        POST    bearer       Save new draft, return token
/preview/<token>                   GET     HMAC token   Render styled preview page
/api/approve/<token>               POST    HMAC token   Flip state, resume n8n
/api/reject/<token>                POST    HMAC token   Flip state, skip post
/api/drafts/<id>/posted            POST    bearer       Mark draft as posted


AUTH MODEL
  - N8N_SECRET:       long random string, shared only between n8n and Flask
  - HMAC_SECRET:      separate secret, used to sign preview tokens
  - Preview token:    HMAC_SHA256(draft_id + expiry, HMAC_SECRET)
  - Token expiry:     24 hours
  - /api/* routes:    reject anything without bearer token
  - Rate limit:       /api/approve/* capped at 5 requests/min


6. DATABASE SCHEMA (SQLite)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CREATE TABLE topics (
  id         INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  category   TEXT,        -- startup | cybersec | coding | corporate
  prompt     TEXT,
  used       INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);

CREATE TABLE drafts (
  id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  topic_id        INTEGER,
  category        TEXT,
  body            TEXT,
  status          TEXT,   -- pending | approved | rejected | posted
  token           TEXT,
  token_expiry    INTEGER,
  n8n_resume_url  TEXT,
  created_at      INTEGER,
  posted_at       INTEGER
);


7. HUMAN EXPERIENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  09:00  Phone buzzes: "New draft ready: Why zero-trust matters..."
  09:01  Tap notification --> browser opens preview page
  09:01  Preview shows styled post + [Approve] [Reject]
  09:02  Tap Approve --> "Approved" page --> n8n posts within seconds

  If no tap:
  09:30  n8n timeout fires --> Gemini proofreads --> posts anyway


8. SECURITY MINIMUMS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  [ ] N8N_SECRET is long, random, unique
  [ ] HMAC_SECRET is separate from N8N_SECRET
  [ ] Preview tokens expire in 24h
  [ ] /api/* rejects requests without bearer token
  [ ] /api/approve/* rate-limited to 5/min
  [ ] Jinja2 autoescape ON (prevents XSS from generated content)
  [ ] SQLite file NOT web-accessible
  [ ] Flask runs behind reverse proxy (nginx/caddy)
  [ ] HTTPS only (Let's Encrypt)


